## Query and Mutation Structure

### Query Organization

#### File Structure
```
frontend-nx/apps/edu-hub/queries/
├── fragments/           # Reusable GraphQL fragments
│   ├── userFragment.ts
│   ├── courseFragment.ts
│   └── sessionFragment.ts
├── queries/            # Read operations
│   ├── user.ts
│   ├── courseList.ts
│   └── myCourses.ts
└── mutations/          # Write operations
    ├── mutateCourse.ts
    └── insertUser.ts
```

#### Fragment Pattern
**Always use fragments for reusable field sets:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Reusable fragment
export const USER_FRAGMENT = gql`
  fragment UserFragment on User {
    id
    firstName
    lastName
    email
    picture
    externalProfile
    zipCode
    country
  }
`;

// ✅ GOOD: Use fragment in queries
export const USER_LIST = gql`
  ${USER_FRAGMENT}
  query UserList {
    User(where: { status: { _eq: ACTIVE } }) {
      ...UserFragment
    }
  }
`;
```

#### Query Naming Conventions
- **Queries**: `ENTITY_LIST`, `ENTITY_BY_ID`, `MY_ENTITIES`
- **Mutations**: `INSERT_ENTITY`, `UPDATE_ENTITY`, `DELETE_ENTITY`
- **Fragments**: `ENTITY_FRAGMENT`, `ENTITY_FRAGMENT_MINIMUM`

### Mutation Patterns

#### Insert Pattern
```typescript
export const INSERT_COURSE = gql`
  mutation InsertCourseWithLocation(
    $title: String!, 
    $applicationEnd: date!, 
    $maxMissedSessions: Int!, 
    $programId: Int!,
    $locationOption: LocationOption_enum!
  ) {
    insert_Course(objects: {
      title: $title
      tagline: ""
      language: "DE"
      applicationEnd: $applicationEnd
      maxMissedSessions: $maxMissedSessions
      programId: $programId
      CourseLocations: {
        data: {
          locationOption: $locationOption
          defaultSessionAddress: ""
        }
      }
    }) {
      affected_rows
      returning {
        id
        CourseLocations {
          id
        }
      }
    }
  }
`;
```

#### Update Pattern
```typescript
export const UPDATE_COURSE = gql`
  mutation UpdateCourse($id: Int!, $updates: Course_set_input!) {
    update_Course_by_pk(pk_columns: { id: $id }, _set: $updates) {
      id
      title
      updated_at
    }
  }
`;
```

## Authentication and Authorization

> **💡 Tip**: See [Frontend Component Patterns](frontend-component-patterns.mdc) for component integration examples and [Testing Standards](testing-standards.mdc) for GraphQL testing patterns.

### Role-Based Hooks

#### Available Hooks
```typescript
// For admin operations
const { data, loading, error } = useAdminQuery(QUERY, options);

// For instructor operations  
const { data, loading, error } = useInstructorQuery(QUERY, options);

// For authenticated user operations
const { data, loading, error } = useAuthedQuery(QUERY, options);

// For role-based mutations
const [mutation] = useAdminMutation(MUTATION, options);
const [mutation] = useInstructorMutation(MUTATION, options);
const [mutation] = useAuthedMutation(MUTATION, options);
```

#### Hook Usage Pattern
```typescript
import { useAdminQuery, useRoleMutation } from '../../hooks/authedMutation';

const MyComponent = () => {
  // Query with proper typing
  const { data, loading, error } = useAdminQuery<QueryResult>(QUERY, {
    variables: { id },
    skip: !id, // Skip query if no ID
  });

  // Mutation with error handling
  const [mutation] = useRoleMutation<MutationResult>(MUTATION, {
    onCompleted: (data) => {
      // Handle success
      refetch(); // Refetch related queries
    },
    onError: (error) => {
      console.error('Mutation error:', error);
      // Handle error
    },
    refetchQueries: ['QueryName'], // Auto-refetch
  });
};
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Standard Error Handling

#### Component-Level Error Handling
```typescript
import { ErrorMessageDialog } from '../common/dialogs/ErrorMessageDialog';

const MyComponent = () => {
  const [errorMessage, setErrorMessage] = useState('');
  const [errorOpen, setErrorOpen] = useState(false);

  const [mutation] = useRoleMutation(MUTATION, {
    onError: (error) => {
      console.error('GraphQL Error:', error);
      setErrorMessage(error.message);
      setErrorOpen(true);
    },
  });

  return (
    <>
      {/* Component content */}
      <ErrorMessageDialog
        errorMessage={errorMessage}
        open={errorOpen}
        onClose={() => setErrorOpen(false)}
      />
    </>
  );
};
```

#### Specific Error Handling
```typescript
// Handle specific constraint errors
const handleAliasError = useCallback(
  (error: ApolloError) => {
    // Check for duplicate alias constraint error
    if (error.message.includes('already exists in organization')) {
      const match = error.message.match(/Alias "([^"]+)" already exists in organization "([^"]+)"/);
      if (match) {
        const [, aliasName, orgName] = match;
        onError(
          t('error.alias_already_exists', {
            alias: aliasName,
            organization: orgName,
          })
        );
        return;
      }
      onError(t('error.alias_duplicate_error'));
      return;
    }
    // Default error message
    onError(t('error.alias_update_failed'));
  },
  [onError, t]
);
```

### Authentication Error Handling
```typescript
const useErrorHandler = () => {
  const { t } = useTranslation();

  return (error) => {
    console.log('error handler error: ', error);
    if (error.message.includes('JWTExpired') || error.message.includes('JWSInvalidSignature')) {
      alert(t("authed_query.session_expired_or_invalid"));
      signOut();
    } else {
      alert(t("authed_query.authentication_error") + ": " + error);
    }
  };
};
```

## Caching Strategies

### Apollo Client Cache Management

#### Refetch Patterns
```typescript
// Manual refetch
const { data, loading, refetch } = useAdminQuery(QUERY);
await refetch();

// Auto-refetch after mutations
const [mutation] = useRoleMutation(MUTATION, {
  refetchQueries: ['QueryName', 'AnotherQuery'],
});

// Conditional refetch
const [mutation] = useRoleMutation(MUTATION, {
  onCompleted: (data) => {
    if (data.success) {
      refetch();
    }
  },
});
```

#### Cache Updates
```typescript
// Update cache after mutation
const [mutation] = useRoleMutation(MUTATION, {
  update: (cache, { data }) => {
    // Update specific cache entry
    cache.modify({
      id: cache.identify({ __typename: 'Course', id: courseId }),
      fields: {
        title: () => data.updateCourse.title,
      },
    });
  },
});
```

## Component Integration Patterns

### Input Field Integration
```typescript
// Standard input field with GraphQL mutation
<InputField
  variant="material"
  type="text"
  label={t('course.title')}
  value={course.title}
  updateValueMutation={UPDATE_COURSE_TITLE}
  itemId={course.id}
  onValueUpdated={(data) => {
    // Handle successful update
    showSuccessMessage(t('course.title_updated'));
  }}
  refetchQueries={['CourseList', 'CourseDetails']}
/>
```

### Table Integration with useTableGrid
```typescript
const { data, loading, error, searchFilter, pageIndex, setSearchFilter, setPageIndex } = useTableGrid({
  queryHook: useAdminQuery,
  query: COURSE_LIST,
  queryVariables: filter,
  pageSize: filter.limit || 50,
  debounceMs: 1000,
  refetchFilter: useCallback(
    (searchTerm) => {
      const searchWhere = searchTerm ? { title: { _ilike: `%${searchTerm}%` } } : {};
      return {
        where: {
          ...filter.where,
          ...searchWhere,
        },
      };
    },
    [filter.where]
  ),
});
```

### Optimistic Updates
```typescript
const [mutation] = useRoleMutation(MUTATION, {
  optimisticResponse: {
    updateCourse: {
      __typename: 'Course',
      id: courseId,
      title: newTitle,
    },
  },
  update: (cache, { data }) => {
    // Update cache with optimistic response
    cache.modify({
      id: cache.identify({ __typename: 'Course', id: courseId }),
      fields: {
        title: () => newTitle,
      },
    });
  },
});
```

## Type Safety

### TypeScript Integration
```typescript
// Define query result types
interface CourseListResult {
  Course: Course[];
  Course_aggregate: {
    aggregate: {
      count: number;
    };
  };
}

// Use typed queries
const { data, loading, error } = useAdminQuery<CourseListResult>(COURSE_LIST, {
  variables: { limit: 50, offset: 0 },
});

// Type-safe data access
const courses = data?.Course || [];
const totalCount = data?.Course_aggregate?.aggregate?.count || 0;
```

